{
  "name": "Ivanti Error Incident Handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Ivanti Error Incident Handler\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Triggers when a workflow error occurs, then waits briefly to avoid immediate reprocessing.\n2. Searches Ivanti Neurons for ITSM for an incident related to the error context.\n3. If no related incident exists, creates a new incident.\n4. If an incident exists, checks whether it is resolved.\n5. If resolved, reactivates the incident and then appends a note; otherwise, just appends a note.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Configure the Error Trigger node (or ensure this workflow is set as the error workflow) so it receives error events from your main workflows.\n- - [ ] Set the Wait node duration appropriate for your incident system’s rate limits and eventual consistency needs.\n- - [ ] Add Ivanti Neurons for ITSM credentials (base URL/tenant + auth) and select them in all Ivanti nodes (Find Related Incident, Create New Incident, Set Status Active, Insert Note).\n- - [ ] Configure the Ivanti queries/fields: define how “related incident” is identified, which fields are set on create, what status value maps to “Active”, and the note content format.\n- - [ ] Review both IF nodes’ conditions to match your Ivanti response structure (no results vs results, and resolved vs not resolved).\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can change the correlation logic in “Find Related Incident” (e.g., by workflow name, error message hash, or service/component), and adjust the “Insert Note” content to include stack traces, execution IDs, and links back to n8n.",
        "height": 832,
        "width": 480
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -128,
        96
      ],
      "id": "03619783-cd01-4e86-9f91-7d86b84ecd56",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
